phy: tegra: xusb-tegra210: no stack overflow for a lane without a USB 3 port

The PCIe and SATA PHY power-on formats "prod_c_ss%d" with the lane's USB 3
port into an 11-byte stack buffer. A lane mapped to no USB 3 port, such as
the Nano's PCIe Ethernet lane, has port -EINVAL: "prod_c_ss-22" needs 13
bytes, and the stack protector panics ("Kernel stack is corrupted in:
tegra210_pcie_phy_power_on"). R35 ships only for Tegra186 and newer, where
this Tegra210 code never runs.

Only lanes mapped to a USB 3 port now look up prod settings, with a 16-byte
buffer and snprintf.

Found: trial 2, a panic early in the boot.
Tested on the Nano: trial 3 got through every driver.

Licence: GPL-2.0-only. Lab notes, with every measurement: NOTES.md.
---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
index a65423111..479269306 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra210.c
@@ -2828,10 +2828,16 @@ static int tegra210_pcie_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 
 	mutex_lock(&padctl->lock);
 
-	if (priv->prod_list) {
-		char prod_name[] = "prod_c_ssX";
+	/*
+	 * Only lanes mapped to a USB3 port have prod_c_ss settings. Any other
+	 * lane (the Nano's PCIe Ethernet lane) used to print -EINVAL as "-22"
+	 * past the end of an 11-byte buffer and trip the stack protector.
+	 */
+	if (priv->prod_list && tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane) >= 0) {
+		char prod_name[16];
 
-		sprintf(prod_name, "prod_c_ss%d", tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane));
+		snprintf(prod_name, sizeof(prod_name), "prod_c_ss%d",
+			 tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane));
 
 		err = tegra_prod_set_by_name(&padctl->regs, prod_name,
 				priv->prod_list);
@@ -3011,10 +3017,12 @@ static int tegra210_sata_phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 
 	mutex_lock(&padctl->lock);
 
-	if (priv->prod_list) {
-		char prod_name[] = "prod_c_ssX";
+	/* As in tegra210_pcie_phy_power_on(): USB3-mapped lanes only. */
+	if (priv->prod_list && tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane) >= 0) {
+		char prod_name[16];
 
-		sprintf(prod_name, "prod_c_ss%d", tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane));
+		snprintf(prod_name, sizeof(prod_name), "prod_c_ss%d",
+			 tegra210_usb3_lane_map(lane));
 		err = tegra_prod_set_by_name(&padctl->regs, prod_name,
 				priv->prod_list);
 		if (err)
